ish Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:da79468e2f4a21cf2b","definition":"Fine champagne; French brandy.","example":"We had dined at l'Avenue's, and afterward went to the Café de Versailles for coffee. We had several fines after the coffee, and I said I must be going.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["filing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5f166005e2f544de5d","definition":"Something that is fine; fine particles.","example":"They filtered silt and fines out of the soil.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"plural-normally","register":"plural-normally","wordFamily":["filing"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d324f4cb602e51bfc8","definition":"To make finer, purer, or cleaner; to purify or clarify.","example":"to fine gold","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a342600819e02e273","definition":"To become finer, purer, or cleaner.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["clarify","refine","purify"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8