r littering, but she appealed.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amerce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite","bar fine","fineless","The Fine City","finable","fineable","unfined"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3c7c9599f47c196c09","definition":"To pay a fine.","example":"Men fined for the king's good will; or that he would remit his anger; women fined for leave to marry.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["amerce"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite","bar fine","fineless","The Fine City","finable","fineable","unfined"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4fadf923b03d7e64db","definition":"The end of a musical composition.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite","bar fine","fineless","The Fine City","finable","fineable","unfined","da capo al fine=D.C. al fine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fine#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3dc2fa369dde0b4eb1","definition":"The location in a musical score that indicates the end of the piece, particularly when the piece ends somewhere in the middle of the score due to a section of the music being repeated.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["filing","final","finite","bar fine","fineless","The Fine City","finable","fineable","unfined","da capo al fine=D.C. al fine"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.